+\subsubsection{Comparison of Precipitation-Appropriate Likelihoods}
+\label{sec:r2m6_likelihood_results}
+
+In the matched likelihood reruns, full CRPS was 0.0961 for Gaussian, 0.0847 for Tobit and 0.0773~mm\,h$^{-1}$ for Bernoulli--Gamma. Relative to Gaussian, Bernoulli--Gamma reduced full CRPS by approximately 19.6\%, IS95 by 29\% and Width95 by 32\%; overall Cov95 remained similar (0.9565 versus 0.9560). Both non-negative likelihoods eliminated negative bounds by construction. Bernoulli--Gamma increased upper-tail Cov95 from 0.4941 to 0.6445, still far below 0.95; Tobit gave 0.5454. The observed upper-tail reliability deficit was therefore reduced but not resolved.
+
+Part B of Table~\ref{tab:probabilistic_results} reports these reruns separately from Part A1; Part A2 uses the existing q16 interval reruns. Supplementary Tables~\ref{supp-stab:r2m6_seed_scores} and~\ref{supp-stab:r2m6_seed_intervals} give per-seed evidence; Tables~\ref{supp-stab:r2m6_score_pairs} and~\ref{supp-stab:r2m6_other_pairs} retain both uncertainty summaries.
+
+Bernoulli--Gamma reduced the Q95 and 1.0~mm\,h$^{-1}$ threshold-weighted CRPS by only about 2.8\% and 1.9\%, respectively, on all test cases. Its full CRPS was lower than Tobit under both paired uncertainty summaries, but their high-threshold block intervals included zero despite seed-$t$ intervals excluding zero. The historical observed-wet and upper-tail conditional CRPS diagnostics instead ranked Bernoulli--Gamma worse than Gaussian; these outcome-conditioned diagnostics are not proper scores for the full predictive distribution. We retain this adverse result separately from the full/twCRPS comparison.
+
+Tobit was more sensitive to the explored dry definitions than Bernoulli--Gamma. The dry $=0.001$ five-seed full scores are retained alongside the main setting; a matching Tobit dry-0.001 minus dry-0 full block interval was not saved and is not inferred from approximate-CRPS intervals. The dry $=0.01$ result is only a historical seed-42 exploration, not a five-seed robustness result. Historical validation CRPS did not favour dry $=0$ for either family.
+
+Supplementary Tables~\ref{supp-stab:r2m6_dry001}--\ref{supp-stab:r2m6_conditional_history} separate the five-seed sensitivity from historical single-seed and conditional-score diagnostics.
